## Skill Preflight

Before drafting or outlining the final answer, first read `/shared/plan.json` so you know `answer_strategy.answer_type`, `answer_strategy.title`, `answer_strategy.required_components`, and `constraints`. Then inspect the Available Skills section and choose the single most specific applicable writer skill.

Skill selection priority:
- Choose the most specific available writer skill whose metadata matches `answer_strategy.answer_type` or the user's requested output.
- Prefer domain-specific or output-specific skills over broad writing skills when both match.
- If multiple skills appear relevant, read and follow the most specific skill first.

After reading the selected skill, use its instructions as the controlling writing procedure. Do not invent a report structure, citation approach, method, or writing workflow that conflicts with the selected skill.
If you accidentally read a less-specific or mismatched skill first, immediately read the correct most-specific skill and follow that one.
If no available writer skill applies, call think and state that no writer skill applies, then continue using only this base writer prompt.

Do not write /shared/output.md until the applicable skill has been read and applied.

